{{- define "package-doc" -}}
{{- $iface := .IfaceName -}}
{{- $driver := .DriverName -}}
// Package {{ .PackageName }} measures performance characteristics of
// any implementation of [{{ .Spec.QualifiedType }}]. Generated by
// `testkit bench`.
//
// # Usage
//
//	func BenchmarkStore(b *testing.B) {
//	    {{ $driver }}(b, func() {{ .QualifiedTypeForTest }} {
//	        return newInMemory()
//	    })
//	}
//
// # Default-emitted primitives
//
// Every non-skipped method gets:
//   - <Method>/hot-path                    — single-goroutine ns/op + allocs/op
//
// Methods whose shape is concurrency-safe also get
// <Method>/concurrent-4 (multi-goroutine throughput). Lifecycle,
// VoidLifecycle, and Unknown shapes default to hot-path only —
// concurrent invocation of Init/Reset/Close on a shared impl is
// rarely safe. Consumers needing concurrent measurement on those
// methods supply a typed primitive through the per-method plug-in
// slot.
//
// # Opt-in CI gates
//
// Two directives turn on deterministic budget enforcement:
//
//	//testkit:allocs N           — fail when allocs/call exceeds N
//	//testkit:latency 100us      — fail when ns/op exceeds the budget
//
// Methods carrying the directives get an additional <Method>/allocs-within-N
// or <Method>/latency-within-D subtest that fails the benchmark on
// budget violation. Methods without the directives skip the gates —
// the budget is a consumer assertion, not an opinionated default.
//
// # Plug-in primitives
//
// Consumers extend each method's bench surface via
// `{{ $iface }}BenchOn<Method>(...)` — typed bench primitives wired
// to the same per-shape Context the always-emitted primitives use.
// Example:
//
//	{{ $driver }}(b, factory,
//	    {{ $iface }}BenchOnGet(bench.ReaderHotPath[T, K, V]("alt-key")),
//	)
//
// # PrePopulate seeder
//
// `{{ $iface }}BenchPrePopulate(fn)` registers a one-shot seeder that
// runs against every freshly-factory'd impl before per-method
// benchmarks observe it. Use it for cache warm-ups, fixture loading,
// or any setup the contract treats as out-of-band.
//
// # Custom sub-benchmarks
//
// `{{ $iface }}BenchCustom(name, fn)` adds a free-form sub-benchmark
// for measurements outside the shape vocabulary — multi-method
// scenarios, end-to-end flows, etc.
//
// # Coverage summary
//
//   Methods covered:        {{ .CoveredMethodCount }}{{ if gt .SkippedMethodCount 0 }} ({{ .SkippedMethodCount }} skipped via //testkit:integration-only){{ end }}
//   Shapes:                 {{ .ShapeBreakdown }}
//   Always-emitted:         hot-path, concurrent-4
//   Plug-in points:         {{ range $i, $name := .PlugInPoints }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}{{ $name }}{{ end }}
{{ end -}}
